  "context": "Step of the corpus rule remediation plan (crr-00-corpus-rule-remediation-plan). Plan written 2026-11-22 and reviewed twice by an independent adversarial reviewer; counts marked (R) were measured by that reviewer and must be re-measured, not trusted. Owner decisions were given by choice dialog on 2026-11-22 and are quoted in crr-00.\n\n2026-11-23 r4 landing reviews (trusted local reviewer) refused five heads; each round found real defects now fixed or in progress: unreadable single-line fixtures named after platforms (replaced by test-time builders); TPC-H power without RF1/RF2 and TPC-DS throughput double counting (fixed to match runtime); combined-metric evidence checks duplicated (now one implementation shared by runtime and corpus); composites gated on requested/stamped class (T1, removed); missing scale/gateway refusal in the corpus composite score, publish/submit gates deciding from the stamp, run.streams overwritten (in progress). Score gate holds throughout: 91 ranked rows compared, max deviation 0.0955%, no rank change.",
  "description": "## Problem\nThe writer omits Power@Size when it stamps a run non-standard, so the stamp's effect is frozen in the file (T1). Readers recompute the score from timings only for subscale runs.\n\n## Change\n- The writer (core/results/schema.py, core/tpc_patterns.py, platforms/dataframe/benchmark_mixin.py) calls the rule. It always records the timings needed to recompute the score, and records the executed stream count.\n- It keeps writing the existing compliance_class vocabulary, as information only.\n- One score function recomputes Power@Size and throughput from timings for every lane. validate_corpus.py and the pipeline use it. Nothing reads summary.tpc_metrics.suppressed.\n- Guard: for every stored result and fixture, change or remove each of benchmark.compliance_class, conformance_class, summary.tpc_metrics, execution.official, phases.power_test.power_at_size, benchmark.test_type and summary.validation's recorded class fields (to other valid values), and assert class, lane, score and rank do not change.\n\n## Decision gates\n- If a recomputed score differs from a recorded one by more than 0.5% for any ranked result, stop and report the list; do not tune the formula to fit.\n\n## Guardrails (apply to every item of this plan)\n- Fix the root cause for every platform and benchmark. No rule, exception, label or test may name a platform or a version matrix. Only the pvm-p* items may name Polars, and only to run and stage that run's files.\n- Never edit a stored result file to make it pass. Outcomes change only through the rule.\n- Any change to the outcome of a stored result must show in the committed outcome snapshot diff in the same pull request and be explained in its body.\n- No new stored class value. No reader may decide anything from benchmark.compliance_class, conformance_class or summary.tpc_metrics.suppressed.\n- Paths, line numbers and counts in this plan were read on 2026-11-22 at develop 93f3360. Re-read before editing; report drift, do not guess.\n- AGENTS.md applies: linked worktree, one pull request per item, close at the merged pull request, heavy work only through make heavy-run, no live cloud run without owner approval in that task.\n- At a decision gate, follow the recorded default. If its stop condition is met, stop and report to the owner. Never substitute a different owner decision.\n- Read crr-00-corpus-rule-remediation-plan first: it holds the owner decisions, the rule table and the fault types (T1 to T5).",
